                            <comment id="16766081" author="pkouznet" created="Tue, 12 Feb 2019 14:33:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt; We used to normalize(uppercase) all the schemas even that ones, that had been computed from cache names. I&apos;ve added escaping for all the sql schema names when we are dynamically creating cache configuration for the new table.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16766121" author="pkouznet" created="Tue, 12 Feb 2019 15:06:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Because of that, we used to lookup for existing table and found nothing (search by schema.table_name is case sensitive, and we don&apos;t normalize schema in that place) then, we tried to create new one, but we couldn&apos;t: there is existing QueryEntity (which we could find because of name normalization in that place).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
